-- =====================================================================
-- spawner control panel
-- ender io powered spawner switchboard for cc: tweaked (mc 1.12.2)
--
-- installation:
--   * place an advanced computer near your spawners
--   * copy this file onto it as "startup" (drop it into
--     saves/<world>/computercraft/computer/<id>/startup, or run
--     "edit startup" in-game and paste it)
--   * reboot the computer; the panel starts automatically and
--     re-applies every saved spawner state to its redstone output
--     (a reboot resets all outputs to off, which is why this file
--     must be named "startup")
--
-- hardware:
--   * required: one advanced computer (colour + arrow keys)
--   * optional: an advanced monitor for a touch panel. place it
--     touching the computer or connect it over wired modems. a basic
--     monitor also works but is display-only (no touch).
--   * optional: a second monitor. when one is present the utilities
--     move onto it and the first monitor shows only the spawners. the
--     two lowest-named monitors are used (first = spawners, second =
--     utilities)
--   * optional: plethora redstone integrators for spawners that are
--     not adjacent to the computer itself
--
-- adding your first integrator:
--   1. place a redstone integrator against the ender io powered
--      spawner. integrators emit on absolute sides:
--      up/down/north/south/east/west
--   2. connect the integrator and the computer with wired modems and
--      networking cable, then right-click each modem so it lights red
--   3. on the panel press A (settings) -> manage integrators ->
--      scan for integrators, and add the one that appears
--      (e.g. "redstone_integrator_0")
--   4. back in settings, add a spawner, set its target to that
--      integrator, pick the side that faces the spawner, and set
--      "inverted" to match the spawner's own redstone mode
--
-- controls (terminal): up/down select, space toggle, tab toggles all
--   at once (master switch: anything on -> all off, else all on),
--   T turns the selected spawner on for a preset duration (with a live
--   countdown), M cycles the persistent default timer (Off, 1m, 5m,
--   ... 2h) that every toggle-on uses, A (or S) opens settings,
--   ctrl+t quits. in menus: enter selects, backspace goes back. text
--   entry: enter accepts, backspace on an empty field cancels.
-- controls (advanced monitor): tap a row to toggle it, tap
--   [ Toggle All ] for the master switch, tap [ Timer: ... ] to cycle
--   the default timer. settings are terminal-only. the monitor picks
--   the largest text scale that still fits the list. utilities render
--   dimmed and, to save vertical space, two per row where width allows.
--   [ Toggle All ] and [ Timer: ... ] share one bottom row on wide
--   monitors and stack on narrow ones. a dedicated utilities monitor
--   renders a touch smaller than the spawner monitor.
--
-- per-item options (settings -> item): item type spawner/utility
--   (utilities are grouped below the spawners and anchor above the
--   monitor's buttons, and render slightly dimmed), interval mode (while
--   on, the output pulses n seconds on / n seconds off; the row still
--   reads ON but shades faintly during the off half), ignore timer
--   (always stays on, no countdowns ever attach), bypass toggle all (the
--   master switch skips it), move up/down to reorder. reordering also
--   works bios-style in the settings list itself: select an item and
--   press + / - to move it.
-- integrators can be given labels (settings -> manage integrators ->
--   pick one -> set label). the header bar colour is also picked in
--   settings. everything persists in the config file.
--
-- config lives in "config" next to this program; a corrupt file is
-- moved to "config.bak" and the panel starts fresh.
-- =====================================================================

